val -- Evaluate an XMLnode containing OpenMath
**********************************************

  * Usage: 
        val x
  * Inputs:
      * x
  * Outputs:
      * the value of the OpenMath object described by x

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : t = parse ///<OMA><OMS cd="arith1"                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = <OMA                                                                    |
|       <OMS cd="arith1" name="plus"                                          |
|       <OMI "1"                                                              |
|       <OMI "2"                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : XMLnode                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|name="plus"/><OMI>1</OMI><OMI>2</OMI></OMA>///                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : val t                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = 3                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note openMath: openMath, -- Turn an arbitrary Macaulay2 object into
    OpenMath (if possible)

Ways to use val:
================

  * "val(XMLnode)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note val: val, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

